The class `ObservableIgnoreElements` is a thin wrapper that forwards subscription events and discards `onNext` values without any computational work. Its behavior is essentially a no‑op for the data path, and the performance characteristics are already covered by RxJava’s existing operator benchmarks. Adding a dedicated JMH benchmark would provide little additional insight and would duplicate effort already present in the library’s test suite. Therefore, generating a new JMH benchmark is unnecessary.